<title>USA: GM says idle workers now total 18,371.</title>
<headline>GM says idle workers now total 18,371.</headline>
<dateline>WARREN, Mich. 1996-10-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>General Motors Corp said on Monday it had idled 18,371 assembly and parts plant workers in the U.S. and Mexico because of the strike by Canadian auto workers.</p>
<p>The number is up 10,893 from Friday and includes elimination of some shifts at four car assembly plants in the U.S. -- in Orion Township, Mich.; Fairfax, Kansas; Wentzville, Mo., and Lansing Mich.</p>
<p>Also now idle are 2,050 workers at GM's transmission plant in Warren, Mich., and more than 1,000 workers at other parts plants that state.</p>
<p>GM said it would issue an update at 1600 EDT/2000 GMT today.</p>
